            "qa": [
              {
                "title": "Q1561 (Sep. 19, 2025)",
                "question": "If an amulet that has become a follower via Maneuver has its attack or defense changed, does it retain those changes if its Maneuver ability is activated next turn?",
                "answer": "No. When a card's Maneuver ability is activated, its attack and defense become the numbers listed."
              },
              {
                "title": "Q1560 (Sep. 19, 2025)",
                "question": "If an amulet that has become a follower via Maneuver gains Aura, does it retain Aura when it returns to being an amulet at the end of the turn?",
                "answer": "Yes, it does."
              },
              {
                "title": "Q1559 (Sep. 19, 2025)",
                "question": "What does \"Maneuver this card\" mean?",
                "answer": "Maneuver is an ability that turns the card into a follower for that turn. Its attack and defense are listed on the card.\n\nSimilar to ordinary followers, a card that has been turned into a follower via Maneuver cannot attack on the turn it is put onto the field, unless it has Rush or Storm.\n\nCards that have been on the field for more than a turn can attack enemies as normal once Maneuvered."
              }
            ],
